; Two TIA voices, written around the pitches the chip can actually reach.
;
;     python tools/tracker.py render examples/demo.trk -o demo.wav
;     python tools/tracker.py export examples/demo.trk -o demo.asm
;
; AUDC $C -- tone, div 6 -- is the usual melody voice, and its dividers land
; on C, D, E, F#, A and C in this octave. There is no G at all: AUDF 6 gives
; F#4 and AUDF 5 gives A4, with nothing between them. So this tune is built
; from the notes that exist rather than from a scale that does not, which is
; the whole craft of writing for this chip. `tracker.py notes --audc C` lists
; them, and the tracker warns if you ask for one it has to fake.
;
; ch1 answers an octave down and then holds the bass. The last bars are AUDC
; $8, white noise, which has no pitch -- so its AUDF is written as a raw value.
title Two voices
region ntsc
rate 8
;   ch0        | ch1
C C-4 A        | C C-3 6
C D-4 A        | ...
C E-4 A        | ...
C A-4 A        | C C-3 6
C E-4 A        | ...
C D-4 A        | ...
C C-4 A        | C A-2 6
...            | ...
C E-4 9        | C C-3 5
C A-4 9        | ...
C C-5 9        | C E-3 5
...            | ...
C A-4 9        | C A-2 5
C F#4 9        | ...
C E-4 A        | C C-3 6
...            | ...
C C-4 A        | C C-3 4
8 $04 6        | ...
8 $08 4        | C A-2 4
8 $0C 2        | ...
off            | off
